version: 4.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
keywords:
  - web archive
  - digital preservation
  - source corpus
  - provenance
abstract: >
  Public preservation mirror and source corpus of lukefwalton.com, the
  canonical personal site of Luke F. Walton, generated automatically from the
  site. Every published record is preserved as verbatim Markdown and plain
  HTML with a machine-readable catalog, alongside surface records for the
  site's identity pages, the public entity network, and an asset manifest
  listing every referenced media file with checksum, rights status, archive
  policy and provenance. Media binaries are included only when their recorded
  policy allows it (Luke-controlled photographs, artwork and graphics, FEiN
  material, commissioned artwork, papers, selected masters). Public-internet
  evidentiary captures are retained as documentary evidence with third-party
  rights acknowledged; some referenced assets are intentionally metadata-only.
  Mixed-rights archive: the CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 grant covers Luke F. Walton's
  original material only; copyright in third-party and jointly held material
  remains with its respective owners. See RIGHTS.md for rights and reuse terms.
preferred-citation:
